        "right": "i",
        "description": "Source identity relation for the vulnerability-relevant value."
      },
      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "The chunk prefix scanning loop accepts any byte that is not CR or LF, including non-hex characters. This consumes attacker-controlled bytes from the HTTP chunked body into the prefix length i, which determines how many characters are interpreted as the hex chunk size."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_missing_hex_digit_validation",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "src/http.c",
      "function": "getchunk",
      "line": 964,
      "operands": [
        "i",
        "is_hex_digit(s.ptr[i])"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "i",
        "right": "is_hex_digit(s.ptr[i])"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_root_hex_validation",
      "fine_trace_step": 3,
      "description": "The boundary check s.len < i + n + 4 is intended to verify the chunk fits in the buffer. When n is near SIZE_MAX (due to non-hex characters producing overflowed nibble accumulation), the addition i + n + 4 wraps to a small value via unsigned 64-bit overflow, causing the check to pass despite n being astronomical."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_sink_memmove_uses_overflowed_dl",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "src/http.c",
      "function": "deliver_chunked_chunks",
      "line": 997,
      "operands": [
        "dl",
        "n"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "dl",
        "right": "n"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_n_reaches_memmove_dl",
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "memmove uses the inflated chunk data length dl (equal to n from getchunk) as the byte count. Since n is near SIZE_MAX, this reads far beyond the allocated receive buffer, causing a SEGV."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_guard_bypassed_by_overflow",
      "verified": true,
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "src/http.c",
      "function": "getchunk",
      "line": 964,
      "fine_trace_step": 3,
      "state": "With n=18446744073709551614 (SIZE_MAX-1), the guard expression i + n + 4 wraps unsigned 64-bit arithmetic to 95, which is less than s.len=380. The guard s.len < i + n + 4 evaluates to false, so execution continues despite n being astronomical.",
      "operands": [
        "s.len",
        "n"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "s.len",
        "right": "n"
      },
      "verified_by": "a_n_exceeds_buffer"
    }
  ],
